# Exercise: Capacity Planning
#
# Little's Law lets us turn a throughput target into a worker count.
#
#     L = λ × W   →   K = ceil(L) = ceil(λ_target × W)
#
# Inputs we control or measure:
#   - λ_target — what throughput do we need? (items per second)
#   - W        — how long does one item take? (per-item service time)
#
# Output we derive:
#   - K — how many parallel workers do we need to spawn?
#
# Worked numbers for this exercise:
#   - λ_target = 200 items/sec
#   - W        = 20ms = 20_000us = 0.020 sec
#   - L        = 200 × 0.020 = 4
#   - K        = ceil(4) = 4 workers
#
# We then VERIFY the math: spawn K=4 workers, push K items, measure
# the achieved throughput, and check it meets the 200/sec target
# (with 20% headroom for jitter — assert achieved λ >= 160/sec).
#
# Helper word `spawn-worker` is provided — call it K times.
#
# Your task: spawn 4 workers, run 4 items through them, measure
# elapsed in microseconds, compute achieved λ in items/sec.
# When done, delete the marker line below.


: spawn-worker ( Channel Channel -- Channel Channel )
    [ over chan.receive drop 20 time.sleep-ms 1 i.+ swap chan.send drop drop ] strand.spawn drop
;

: test-capacity-planning ( -- )
    chan.make
    chan.make

    # Stack going in: ( work results )
    # Your code here:
    # - call spawn-worker 4 times (K = 4 from the math above)
    # - take a start timestamp
    # - send 4 items (any values; we just want them processed) —
    #   push the value first, then `3 pick` for work
    # - receive 4 results, discarding values — `1 pick` for results
    # - compute elapsed_us = time.now - start
    # - compute λ_achieved = N × 1_000_000 / elapsed_us
    #   (multiply N by 1_000_000 *before* dividing — integer math)
    # - clean the channels off the stack
    # Stack coming out: ( λ_achieved )   -- items per second

    spawn-worker
    spawn-worker
    spawn-worker
    spawn-worker

    time.now

    10 3 pick chan.send drop
    20 3 pick chan.send drop
    30 3 pick chan.send drop
    40 3 pick chan.send drop

    1 pick chan.receive drop drop
    1 pick chan.receive drop drop
    1 pick chan.receive drop drop
    1 pick chan.receive drop drop

    time.now swap i.-
    4 1000000 i.* swap i./ drop

    nip nip

    # Do not edit below this line
    # Achieved must clear 160 items/sec (80% of the 200/sec target).
    160 i.>= test.assert

;
